  "worked_solution": "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+2v,\\,v-2u) \\\\  & =({0}^{2}+2v,\\,v-2(0)) \\\\  & =(2v,v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2v,\\,y=v,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(2,1)$ and $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114545/assets/0b61f3a91c912dcd042bdd5cc11b0f393a8ea85269ecbef000403cf080166cf7.png)",
